---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";

import CardGroup from "@components/CardGroup.astro";
import Card from "@components/Card.astro";
import TitleText from "@components/starter-kit/TitleText.astro";

import easyAssemblyImg from "./images/easy-assembly.webp";
import codingOptionalImg from "./images/coding-optional.webp";
---

<section class="block-succeed">
  <TitleText>
    <h2 slot="title" class="title">All you need to succeed</h2>
    <p slot="text">
      The starter kit has all the quality components you need for a successful
      build, so you don't have to source them yourself. To bring it all
      together, we’ve created two digital companions to guide you from the first
      connection to your first automation.
    </p>
  </TitleText>

  <CardGroup columns="2fr 1fr">
    <Card span="full" bleed>
      <Image
        slot="media"
        src={easyAssemblyImg}
        alt="Ribbon cable connecting starter kit modules"
      />
      <h3>Easy assembly: Ribbon cable system.</h3>
      <p>
        We've stripped back the complexity so you can focus entirely on
        learning: simply snap the modules off the panel and connect to the
        compute board via a single ribbon cable. No wiring, pins, soldering, or
        risk of getting it wrong!
      </p>
    </Card>
    <Card href="#">
      <Image
        slot="media"
        src={codingOptionalImg}
        alt="Visual device builder interface"
      />
      <h3>Coding optional:<br />Visual device builder</h3>
      <p>
        Intuitive interface lets you configure hardware and firmware without
        writing code – but the YAML's always there underneath, should you want
        it! Runs on your desktop via our app, or on your existing smart home
        setup.
      </p>
    </Card>
    <Card href="#">
      <h3>Guided support:<br />Learning Wiki</h3>
      <p>
        More than just assembly instructions, our Wiki explains the “why” behind
        each action. It shows how your components connect to the code running
        them, giving you the skills to take on bigger projects when you're
        ready.
      </p>
    </Card>
  </CardGroup>
</section>

<style lang="scss"></style>
